/*******************************************************************************
* djinterp [c][math]                                                    scalar.h
*
* Scalar helpers: abs, copysign, is_finite, min, max, min_num, max_num,
* clamp, lerp, ldexp and frexp, for float, double and long double, as the
* owner's ruling 13 has them (2026.11.24).
*   GENERATED by scripts/gen_c_math_float.py from one text for the three
* families: edit the generator, not this file.
*
*   Each is exact, so each answers to the bit on every platform. min and
* max are IEEE 754-2019's minimum and maximum: a NaN in gives NaN out,
* and -0 is less than +0, as the expression language's are (S338).
* min_num and max_num pass a NaN over for the other number, as C23's
* fminimum_num does. clamp keeps a NaN. lerp is exact at both ends and
* never past them, as C++20's is. abs, copysign, is_finite, ldexp and
* frexp come twice, as in nearest_integer.h: the _c form pure arithmetic,
* a constant expression from C++14, and the plain form the C library's,
* the two agreeing bit for bit; the rest, which C99 lacks, once.
*
* HOW TO USE
* ----------
*   Include it from C or C++. d_math_d_abs, _copysign and _is_finite,
* d_math_d_min and _max, IEEE 754-2019's minimum and maximum, d_math_d_min_num
* and _max_num, which pass a NaN over, d_math_d_clamp, d_math_d_lerp, and
* d_math_d_ldexp and _frexp; abs, copysign, is_finite, ldexp and frexp have _c
* forms too. Each name comes for each family, _f, _d and _ld after d_math_, as
* d_math_d_sqrt; in C++ the family's own name, d_math_sqrt, is overloaded on
* the three.
*
* OPTIONS
* -------
*   None: nothing in this header is chosen at run time; the _c form or the
* plain one is the caller's, by name, and both give the same bits.
*
* CONFIGURATION
* -------------
*   None of its own: it compiles as C, and as C++ from ISO strict C++98, where
* copysign and is_finite are the _c forms; every function but the plain forms
* is a constant expression from C++14 (math_common.h's D_MATH_FN). It assumes
* subnormals, as float_order.h does.
*
*
* path:      /inc/djinterp/c/modules/math/scalar.h
* link(s):   TBA
* author(s): Samuel 'teer' Neal-Blim                         created: 2026.11.24
*                                                            revised: 2026.11.24
*******************************************************************************/

